WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 7.8 · Brand, Identity & Image
Brand consistency and governance

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
A few simple brand rules, set now, keep things consistent when others start producing materials.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.281
Brand governance is the light process that keeps your brand consistent without slowing everyone down. When you are one or two people, it can be a few simple rules, set now.

4
00:00:26.681 --> 00:00:27.281
Simple rules to set now

5
00:00:27.281 --> 00:00:37.500
Brand owner: One named person answers for the brand, even if it is you. For example: The co-founder who leads sales owns the brand and its files.

6
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:48.089
Approval levels: What anyone can produce, what needs a second look and what needs approval. For example: Trainees use templates freely; co-branding and press statements need a founder.

7
00:00:48.089 --> 00:00:58.678
Asset library: One shared place for current files; old versions retired at once. For example: One shared folder; last year’s flyer deleted the day the new one arrived.

8
00:00:58.678 --> 00:01:10.837
Annual review: Once a year, check recognition, trust, fit with strategy and consistency. For example: After the first year, ask ten market shoppers what they think of the bakery.

9
00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:11.837
Why it matters

10
00:01:11.837 --> 00:01:16.030
1. Brands wear down through many small inconsistencies.

11
00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:21.333
2. Rules set now are in place before others produce materials.

12
00:01:21.333 --> 00:01:27.267
3. Strategies and audiences change often in the early years.

13
00:01:27.667 --> 00:01:28.267
What it keeps on track

14
00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:32.089
1. Your guidelines and templates, kept current.

15
00:01:32.089 --> 00:01:35.911
2. Materials made by volunteers and partners.

16
00:01:35.911 --> 00:01:41.104
3. Your yearly reviews, alongside your MEAL routine.

17
00:01:41.504 --> 00:01:42.104
What to avoid

18
00:01:42.104 --> 00:01:46.667
Old logos and homemade flyers left in circulation.

19
00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:51.230
Requiring approval for everything, which slows everyone down.

20
00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:56.793
Never reviewing the brand once it is launched.

21
00:01:57.393 --> 00:01:59.193
You set up a simple brand governance routine.

22
00:01:59.193 --> 00:02:03.193
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:04.693 --> 00:02:07.793
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
